      )CHECK BRIEF

      ⍝ )SAVE/)LOAD workspace checksum (see plan.txt): )SAVE appends a
      ⍝ CRC32 comment after </Workspace>; )LOAD verifies it and warns
      ⍝ (but still loads) on a mismatch.
      ⍝
      )CLEAR
CLEAR WS

      )DROP checksum_test.xml
³

      )WSID checksum_test
WAS CLEAR WS

      X←'hello'

      ⍝ case 1: unmodified round-trip -- no WARNING. checksum_test.xml
      ⍝ resolves (via the default library path) to workspaces/checksum_test.xml
      ⍝ -- the raw ⎕FIO calls below use that same resolved path so they edit
      ⍝ the exact same file that )SAVE/)LOAD operate on.
      ⍝
      )SAVE checksum_test
20⁰-⁰-⁰  ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰) 

      )LOAD checksum_test.xml
SAVED 20⁰-⁰-⁰ ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰)

      X
hello

      ⍝ case 2: edit a decorative XML comment inside <Workspace> (changes
      ⍝ the checksummed bytes but not the loadability -- comments carry
      ⍝ no meaning) using raw ⎕FIO, then )LOAD again: expect a WARNING
      ⍝ but the workspace shall still load correctly
      ⍝
      data ← ⎕FIO[26] 'workspaces/checksum_test.xml'
      needle ← '<!-- Symbol Table -->'
      pos ← (needle ⍷ data) ⍳ 1
      replacement ← '<!-- Symbol Table (edited) -->'
      new_data ← ((pos-1)↑data) , replacement , (((pos-1)+≢needle)↓data)
      Handle ← 'w' ⎕FIO[3] 'workspaces/checksum_test.xml'
      Wcount ← (⎕UCS new_data) ⎕FIO[7] Handle

      ⎕FIO[4] Handle
0

      ⍝ note: the WARNING itself goes to plain CERR (like the pre-existing
      ⍝ "this workspace was )SAVEd with a VERY..." warning below), which is
      ⍝ not DiffOut-instrumented and therefore not part of the reference
      ⍝ comparison -- only the still-successful )LOAD is verified here.
      ⍝
      )LOAD checksum_test.xml
SAVED 20⁰-⁰-⁰ ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰)

      X
hello

      ⍝ )CHECK_WS: check the on-disk checksum(s) without loading. The
      ⍝ absolute path in the message is not deterministic across checkouts,
      ⍝ so it is swallowed by ³; checksum_test.xml still has the mismatch
      ⍝ from case 2 above (the )LOAD WARNING is CERR-only and doesn't fix
      ⍝ the file on disk). checksum_test.apl doesn't exist, so only one
      ⍝ line (for the .xml) is reported.
      ⍝
      )CHECK_WS checksum_test
WARNING - ³

      )SAVE checksum_test
20⁰-⁰-⁰  ⁰:⁰:⁰ (GMT⁵⁰) 

      )CHECK_WS checksum_test
OK      - ³

      )CHECK_WS no_such_checksum_test_ws
no_such_checksum_test_ws: no such workspace file(s)+

      )DROP checksum_test.xml
